# Selfie: a show that draws its own tree — a leaf red, a stem green, a fork
# blue, edges grey — and slides the board's 25 × 25 window over all of it, a
# pixel a frame, a strip of 25 rows at a time from the top down.
#
# program draws self, the tree it is given: on the stage it lays self out and
# plans the window's way over it (layout.lamb, tour.lamb), and each frame it
# draws what the window shows (window.lamb), counting with num.lamb and
# columns.lamb. The board runs the generated selfie, a much smaller tree the
# generator makes of program that acts as it, given itself by fix: the tree it
# draws is the one running. Below: the show, its picture, the image to flash,
# and a page of its way (page.lamb).
#
# The larger helpers used throughout are bound once, by program, and passed to
# what uses them, the most used last: a name used in many definitions would be
# copied into each. The generated selfie unpacks the program on the board
# before it starts, and a variable costs more there the further out it is
# bound; the orders throughout are the ones that made it smallest and quickest
# to start.
#
# Evaluation is eager: a part that uses none of a λ's variables is worked out
# before the λ is applied. So a branch is given what it goes on with only once
# it is chosen, or the board would work out the rest of every branch.

# [program self i]: the stage, the tour; then the window. The helpers follow
# the body, the last bound first.
program = \self
  (\church (\nl (\inc (\dec (\le (\iter (\b1 (\n31 (\cdec (\cinc (\n25 (\foldr (\nz
    \_ Pair.match (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.window nl iter b1 n25 foldr inc dec church)
      (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.tour self nz b1 cdec cinc nl le n31 n25 foldr iter inc dec church))
    (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.nz n31 dec church))
    List.foldr)
    (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.n25 iter))
    (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.cinc n31 inc))
    (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.cdec n31 dec))
    (dec b1))
    (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.b1 iter))
    Pico.Matrix.Selfie.iter)
    (Pico.Matrix.Selfie.le inc dec church))
    Pico.Matrix.Selfie.dec)
    Pico.Matrix.Selfie.inc)
    Pico.Matrix.Selfie.nl)
  Pico.Matrix.Selfie.church

# ── The generated selfie ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_packed = Generator.compress program
generated = Generator.expand _packed
_selfie = fix generated
# The show: on the board, slewing by 128 since the view moves with it, at 9.8
# frames a second, what the board manages.
_fps = 98
show = Pico.Matrix.show_staged 128 _fps _selfie
# The program; packed, and expanded; the selfie.
_to_string = \l List.join " " $ List.map Nat.to_string l
[size program; size _packed; size generated; size _selfie]
# = 50835 9336 9405 9442

# What it draws, 6.1 s of it:
Pico.Matrix.svg "selfie.svg" 60 show
# = selfie.svg image/svg+xml 187394 bytes sha256:3bf8119e3752000ecbbaf2e9c55c28b842b702969f80ba48c951265d43da0dcc
# The image to flash:
Pico.Matrix.flash "selfie.uf2" [show]
# = selfie.uf2 application/octet-stream 39936 bytes sha256:744169a0a030015deddd7b27cb4cf4f5dde6ceb4593379bf8e24681a1ed7d9ad

# Its way over its own tree, as a page:
file "selfie.html" "text/html" $ Pico.Matrix.Selfie.page _fps _selfie
# = selfie.html text/html 48209 bytes sha256:8e54a2bd1a1bed4cc40b950f76144fe41e638ac0c557a535764fb40737aa90bf
